# MIXINv2's BinNat library in the mixin encoding of inheritance
# (corpora/contest_mixin_library.pl, the library `binary`): problems of
# the reduction series, ported from the retired labeled points of
# contest_inheritance_binary.pl. Each program is the labeled one's, read
# at the same member: C.equality(A.plus(B)) or C.equality(A.times(B)),
# read at church, whose answer is one Boolean.
#
# THE LIBRARY. A binary natural is zero, even 2h carrying its half h, or
# odd 2h + 1 carrying its half_of_predecessor h, least significant bit
# outermost, so a numeral of n bits nests n instances; plus recurses on
# the receiver's halves with increment for the carry of odd + odd, times
# on the receiver's halves, 2h m = h m + h m and (2h + 1) m = (h m + h m)
# + m, h m read twice as the labeled port read it, and equality compares
# bit by bit through the visitor.
#
# THE EQUATIONS, the labeled family's, every sum and product checked with
# Prolog's integers:
# - sums that hold: 13 + 29 = 42, 12345 + 54321 = 66666, 123456789 +
#   987654321 = 1111111110;
# - sums that do not, the right-hand side off by one high bit, so that
#   the comparison must reach it: 13 + 29 = 74, 1000 + 2000 = 5048,
#   123456789 + 987654321 = 2184852934;
# - products: 7 * 6 = 42; 12345678 * 87654321; 123456789012 *
#   210987654321; 12345678901234 * 43210987654321
#   (contest_inheritance_middle_sizes.pl); 1234567890123456 *
#   6543210987654321;
# - and two products smaller than the labeled family's, 2 * 3 = 6 and
#   3 * 3 = 9, so that the family has points weak_head reads: times reads
#   h m twice at every level, which doubles its work at every bit of the
#   receiver when nothing is shared.
#
# THE SNAPSHOT of each is the Boolean of the equation. PROOF:
# plus, times and equality descend on the finite halves under every
# choice, and every class has one implementation of each slot it is read
# at, so every end is the Boolean of the equation.
#
# LIMITS: the family's, 10 s, 256 MB, 256 MB.

#   binary_point(?Point, ?Operation, ?Left, ?Right, ?Result)
#
# Each text is from_cbor of a string literal, a Scott list of bytes,
# imported from corpora/library/text/cbor. Each number is from_cbor of an
# integer literal, a Scott integer, imported from corpora/library/integer/cbor.
# FIXME: the imports project "corpora" https://github.com/Atry/private-overlay/issues/1923
# off the variable gezi, the name of the project root's own
# directory; it breaks if that directory is renamed.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "list")
λ nil cons _ _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "text") "cbor")
λ text_from_cbor _ _ _
. (λtuple. tuple λ. text_from_cbor λx. x)
λ text
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "integer") "cbor")
λ integer_from_cbor _
. (λtuple. tuple λ. integer_from_cbor λx. x)
λ integer
. export
